From: Wi-Fi Aware project
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7925: enable hardware A-MSDU for NAN data

PCIe disables software A-MSDU because it advertises hardware offload.
Admit NAN_DATA to the existing station TLV path, honoring the peer limit
copied from the NMI station and the existing ADDBA A-MSDU veto.
No change to management frames, aggregation size, or peer capabilities.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mcu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mcu.c
@@ -1880,8 +1880,10 @@
 	struct sta_rec_amsdu *amsdu;
 	struct tlv *tlv;
 
+	/* NAN_DATA inherits negotiated aggregation limits from its NMI peer. */
 	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION &&
-	    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
+	    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+	    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA)
 		return;
 
 	if (!link_sta->agg.max_amsdu_len)
